 "nl": [
  "Permit any TCP port from library to database but deny FTP (TCP 21), Telnet (TCP 23).",
  "Block RDP (TCP 3389), SMB (TCP 445), FTP (TCP 21) from dns-servers to nvr; the rest of any TCP port between them is allowed.",
  "Block PostgreSQL (TCP 5432), MySQL (TCP 3306), RDP (TCP 3389) from guest-wifi to ops; the rest of TCP ports 1024-65535 between them is allowed.",
  "Deny all traffic from nvr to mail (this overrides any public service).",
  "Apart from student-lab on HTTPS (TCP 443); ntp-servers on syslog (UDP 514), all traffic originating in dns-servers must be dropped.",
  "guest-wifi must never reach hr, regardless of any other rule.",
  "No packet from engineering may enter library, even for services open to everyone.",
  "Restrict guest-wifi so that its only permitted destinations are ops on NTP (UDP 123); drop all other traffic it originates.",
  "research is isolated: it may only reach guest-wifi on HTTPS (TCP 443), and nothing else.",
  "Deny all traffic from mail to voip (this overrides any public service).",
  "Allow dns-servers to connect to database using IMAP (TCP 143) and HTTPS (TCP 443) and PostgreSQL (TCP 5432).",
  "No packet from nvr may enter voip, even for services open to everyone.",
  "ntp-servers offers HTTPS (TCP 443) and NTP (UDP 123) to every zone.",
  "Permit TCP ports 1024-65535 from printers to database but deny RDP (TCP 3389).",
  "hr may use any UDP port towards voip, except SNMP (UDP 161), which must be blocked.",
  "guest-wifi must accept HTTP (TCP 80) and MySQL (TCP 3306) from voip."
 ],
